    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7c39
    pr_ref:  # 7c39
    description: "Phase 2 of WI-gudob (umbrella: Priority inert-concept linkers). Phase 1 (error_handler → ERROR_HANDLER entrypoint) shipped in PR #3181 (commit d417436594). This item covers the second-highest producer-count inert concept.\n\n**Concept:** `controller` — 34 producer frameworks (aspnet, rails, laravel, symfony, django, spring-mvc, yii, cakephp, codeigniter, fuelphp, silverstripe, slim, lumen, adonisjs, ember, aurelia, loopback, hapi, koa, egg, meteor, phoenix, play, scalatra, lift, finatra, giraffe, suave, ktor, micronaut, quarkus, javalin, grails).\n\n**Dispatch semantics** (distinct from route_handler.py, which already resolves individual route handler methods to concrete functions):\n\n- A `controller` is a class/module that groups related route handlers under a shared route prefix and shared middleware.\n- The Framework-subcategory dispatch is: *controller class/module → containing route group → per-method route bindings*.\n- Output: `contains_routes` edges from controller symbol to each route_handler symbol that lives inside it, tagged with the shared prefix and shared middleware concepts.\n- This is additive to route_handler.py, not overlapping: route_handler resolves the per-method `VERB /prefix/path → method` binding; this linker adds the `controller ← contains_routes ← method` side so slicing \"all requests touching UsersController\" returns the method set and their concrete URLs.\n\n**Acceptance** (per INV-nimuj):\n\n1. Linker emits `contains_routes` edges on at least 3 bakeoff-cohort repositories across at least 2 frameworks.\n2. docs/CONCEPTS.md's `controller` entry flips from inert to live after running scripts/generate-concepts.\n3. Unit tests covering at least 3 framework YAMLs (suggested: rails, aspnet, django — distinct class-vs-module styles).\n4. 100% coverage in hypergumbo-core.\n5. Add a 'controller' concept-aware test in the bakeoff fixture for one of the enumerated repos, demonstrating the edges flow through slice queries.\n\n**Non-goals:**\n- Nested controllers (`ResourceController < ApplicationController`): if inheritance chains matter for route inheritance, file a follow-up item.\n- URL parameter concretization: covered separately by the HTTP linker; this item only handles the containment relationship, not the template-to-value fill.\n\n**Subcategory:** Framework (framework-specific dispatch — route-group registration in each framework's conventions). Tag: framework_dispatch_linkers.\n\n**Design reference:** route_handler.py already demonstrates the concept-to-edge pipeline for VERB-based route dispatch. Follow the same shape, substituting the `controller` concept and emitting `contains_routes` rather than `routes_to`.\n\n**Validation claim (for awaits_bakeoff_validation tag):** On a bakeoff cohort including at least one Rails/Django/ASP.NET/Spring-MVC repo, controller-class dead-code candidates that are currently flagged (because the class itself has no direct invocation — only its methods are routed) should drop meaningfully. Estimated volume pending empirical scan; numerical target to be set in the PR description."  # 7c39
    fields: {}  # 7c39
